=== DESIGN / EXPECTATIONS ===
Exactly two services without profiles: backend + postgres. Host binds LAN_IP:9100/9200; PostgreSQL has no published host port and an internal per-project DB network.
Default project railway-lan-node-N gives a distinct persistent pgdata volume. One local DB service per host, DB_HOST=postgres DB_PORT=5432; never localhost inside backend.
Existing V1/V2 migrations mounted read-only; only fresh volumes initialize. Existing recovery volumes are preserved, not reseeded. No volume deletion.
Required operator values: NODE_ID, LAN_IP, NODE_PEERS, DB_NAME, DB_PASSWORD, BACKEND_IMAGE. Password stays in local ignored env file; images already loaded (pull_policy=never).
POSIX startup guards: IDs1..5, matching DB name, exactly five unique voter entries at9200 including own LAN_IP. Calls real NodeMain directly; no idle tail fallback.
Backend health checks are LOCAL TCP listeners ONLY; postgres readiness and DB observations do not prove quorum or G6 PASS.
